# Design tokens and UI primitives

## Tokens

Single source: `packages/design-tokens/tokens.json` (`color`, `radius`, `space`, `font`, …).

```text
tokens.json
  → pnpm --filter @default/design-tokens generate
  → src/tokens.css   (generated — do not edit)
  → src/theme.ts     (generated — do not edit)
frontend/app/globals.css   @import tokens + @theme inline semantic aliases
```

After editing `tokens.json`, run `generate`. Saving alone does not regenerate.

- Styles use semantic aliases: `bg-[var(--primary)]`, `text-[var(--muted-foreground)]`, `rounded-[var(--radius)]`.
- No hex, rgb, or raw oklch in feature UI or primitives — add values to `tokens.json`.
- New semantic names need an alias in `frontend/app/globals.css` (or `frontend/src/shared/styles/`) mapping to `--color-*` package vars.
- Marketing **scalar** colors live in `packages/design-tokens/tokens.json` (`marketing` / `marketing-dark`) and are emitted by `pnpm generate:tokens`. Complex **gradients** stay in `frontend/src/shared/styles/marketing.css` and may reference those token vars — do not duplicate scalar hex/oklch in CSS.

## Primitives

```text
import { Button } from "@default/ui/primitives/button";
import { cn } from "@default/ui/lib/cn";
```

- `@default/ui` is presentational only — no fetch, no `@default/hooks`, no app data.
- Reuse an existing primitive before a styled `div` or raw `<button>`.
- Feature-only layout stays in `features/<name>/` or `widgets/`. Promote to `@default/ui` when a second consumer needs the same control.

New primitive: `packages/ui/src/primitives/<name>.tsx`, CSS vars + `cva`/`cn`, then package exports.
